From: Daniel Martin <dmanlfc@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] VideoPlayer: convert formats the renderer lacks with ffmpeg 8

ffmpeg 8 rejects buffersink options once the filter is initialised, so
FilterOpen failed and 10-bit, 4:2:2 and 4:4:4 software frames reached the
GLES renderer unconverted and showed black. Set the formats before init.

Leave plain software decoding to the FFmpeg codec, and convert the frames
a hwaccel falls back to software for in the DRM PRIME codec.

---
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/DVDVideoCodecDRMPRIME.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/DVDVideoCodecDRMPRIME.cpp
@@ -39,6 +39,7 @@
 #include <libavutil/imgutils.h>
 #include <libavutil/opt.h>
 #include <libavutil/pixdesc.h>
+#include <libswscale/swscale.h>
 }
 
